<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.4.1">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://liujh22.github.io/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://liujh22.github.io/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2026-10-28T14:51:28+00:00</updated><id>https://liujh22.github.io/feed.xml</id><title type="html">blank</title><subtitle>A simple, whitespace theme for academics. Based on [*folio](https://github.com/bogoli/-folio) design. </subtitle><entry><title type="html">Cassyni talk: Lighting and circadian cues</title><link href="https://liujh22.github.io/blog/2026/cassyni-lighting-circadian-talk/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Cassyni talk: Lighting and circadian cues"/><published>2026-10-13T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-10-13T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://liujh22.github.io/blog/2026/cassyni-lighting-circadian-talk</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://liujh22.github.io/blog/2026/cassyni-lighting-circadian-talk/"><![CDATA[<p>I presented <strong>Lighting and circadian cues shape locomotor strategies for balance and navigation in larval zebrafish</strong> in Cassyni’s <em>Ecology and evolution seminars</em> series.</p> <p>The talk explores how lighting and circadian cues shape the swimming strategies that larval zebrafish use to maintain balance and navigate their environment.</p> <p>The recording is now available. <a href="https://cassyni.com/events/33NjVU33GSXff6VZrbSDJD">Watch on Cassyni</a> or play it below.</p> <figure> <iframe src="https://cassyni.com/embed/events/33NjVU33GSXff6VZrbSDJD" class="img-fluid rounded z-depth-1" frameborder="0" style="width: 100%; height: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; max-width: 100%; overflow: hidden; border: none" allow="fullscreen; accelerometer; autoplay; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen="" scrolling="auto" width="auto" height="auto" title="Lighting and circadian cues shape locomotor strategies for balance and navigation in larval zebrafish - presented by Jiahuan Liu (Cassyni)"/> </figure> <p>The related paper is now published in <em>Proceedings of the Royal Society B: Biological Sciences</em>.</p> <p><a href="https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2026.1651">Read the paper</a> · <a href="/assets/pdf/rspb.2026.1651.pdf">PDF</a> · <a href="https://doi.org/10.17605/OSF.IO/36TFU">Data</a></p>]]></content><author><name>Jiahuan Liu</name></author><category term="talks"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Watch my Cassyni seminar on balance and navigation in larval zebrafish.]]></summary></entry></feed>